\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For a separable Hilbert space $H$, is there $\delta>0$ such that every pair of separable $C^*$-subalgebras $A,B\subseteq B(H)$ at Kadison--Kastler distance less than $\delta$ are spatially isomorphic? This distance is the Hausdorff distance between their closed unit balls in operator norm; spatial isomorphism means conjugacy by a unitary on $H$.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2012/52}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
